<title>UK: Lufthansa increases flights to Israel.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa increases flights to Israel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa AG said it will operate additional flights to Israel to meet an expected high demand this autumn.</p>
<p>From 15 September to 15 November 1997 the airline will schedule three extra flights from Frankfurt to Tel-Aviv using an Airbus A321, Lufthansa said in a statement. These additions will increase the total number of flights operated between Germany and Israel to 18 from 15 each week.</p>
<p>The two class configuration flights will offer space for three to four tonnes of bellyhold cargo.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
